{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false},"description":"Returns byte-level entropy statistics computed from the exact file snapshot: whole-file Shannon entropy (bits/byte), a Pearson chi-square against a uniform byte distribution, and the arithmetic mean byte value; when the bytes parse as an ELF, PE or Mach-O image, per-section entropy and chi-square over each section's file-backed bytes (SizeOfRawData for PE, section/sh file size elsewhere; uninitialized/NOBITS sections report 0); and, over a caller-sized grid of power-of-two blocks (block_size 256..1048576, default 4096; up to max_blocks, default 4096), the maximal consecutive runs of blocks at or above 7.2 bits (high) and at or below 1.0 bit (low). It does NOT decompress, unpack, decrypt, classify intent, extract keys or recover plaintext, and cannot distinguish compressed from encrypted data. It reads the file once (bounded at 256 MiB) without executing the target, without network and without writing files; CPU is bounded by the block/section limits and cooperative cancellation. Bounded lists (sections, high runs, low runs, blocks) each carry {total,returned,truncated} coverage; non-executable input yields subject format 'file' with empty sections; every unknown, clamp or truncation is stated in limitations.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"examples":[{"path":"/artifacts/application"},{"block_size":65536,"max_blocks":1024,"path":"/artifacts/application"}],"properties":{"block_size":{"default":4096,"description":"Block length in bytes for the entropy profile; a power of two in [256, 1048576]","maximum":1048576,"minimum":256,"type":"integer"},"max_blocks":{"default":4096,"description":"Largest number of blocks scanned; the block grid is truncated beyond this","maximum":65536,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"path":{"description":"Absolute filesystem path to the selected local file","